1. PERMITTED EVALUATION

You may, without charge and without a separate agreement:

  (a) view, read, download and compile this software;
  (b) run it on infrastructure you control, on a test or development network
      carrying no real value, for the sole purpose of evaluating it; and
  (c) conduct security research, review or audit of it, and publish your
      findings.

These permissions exist because software a prospective customer's engineers and
auditors may not read is software they cannot responsibly recommend, and
because security research on a system intended to hold public money should
never require anybody's permission.


2. WHAT REQUIRES A WRITTEN AGREEMENT

Everything else, and in particular:

  (a) operating this software on a network carrying real value, real payments,
